<section class="inner-sec">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">How it works between sessions</div>
  <h2>It captures the consult. You keep the art and the price.</h2>
  <p class="lede">Booking isn't the job here — every piece is custom, so the receptionist's whole purpose is turning a vague message into a brief you can actually act on, in the channels where the work really arrives.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Works the DMs, not just the phone</strong>Instagram and Facebook messages answered in minutes — the channels most studios actually run on, and the ones that go unread longest.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Captures the consult brief</strong>The idea, rough size, placement, colour or black-and-grey, references, budget range and timeline — gathered before it ever reaches you.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Never quotes a price</strong>It explains how you price and what a consult involves, then tells them you'll confirm. No number goes out that you didn't set.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Answers the studio questions</strong>Deposits, shop minimum policy, age and ID, hours, parking, walk-ins versus appointment, whether you're booking at all right now.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Aftercare, from your posted policy</strong>It repeats the aftercare instructions you've published and nothing else. Anything that sounds like a complication goes to a human immediately.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Books consults when you're ready</strong>Start with capture only. Once you trust it, let it put fixed-length consultations straight onto a calendar.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">Who it's built for</div>
  <h2>Studios that run on messages</h2>
  <p class="lede">If the inquiry arrives as a DM while your hands are busy, the fit is the same whatever you tattoo.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Custom tattoo studios</strong>Every piece is quoted individually, so the value isn't booking — it's arriving at the consult already knowing what they want.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Solo &amp; private studios</strong>No front desk at all. You are the artist, the scheduler and the inbox, and the inbox always loses.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Multi-artist shops</strong>Inquiries get captured with style and artist preference, so the right person picks them up instead of everything landing in one pile.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Body piercing</strong>Higher volume, shorter appointments, and constant repeat questions about jewellery, healing times and aftercare — answered from what you've posted.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Cover-ups &amp; rework</strong>The ones that genuinely need your eyes get flagged as consults rather than being half-answered in a DM thread.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Studios with no website</strong>Plenty of shops run entirely on Instagram and Facebook. The receptionist works those channels directly — a site is optional, not a prerequisite.</div>
  </div>
</section>

