<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="proof-band">
    <div class="sec-eyebrow">Where the line is</div>
    <h2>It never speaks for your art</h2>
    <p>A receptionist can gather what you need to know before a consult. It cannot judge whether a design will hold, whether a cover-up will work, or what a piece is worth — and it doesn't pretend to. Those are the reasons someone chose you, and they stay with you.</p>
    <div class="proof-points">
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>No price, ever</strong>
        <span>It captures size, placement and scope and explains how you price. The number is yours, given when you've seen what they're asking for.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>No opinion on the work</strong>
        <span>Whether a design suits a spot, whether a cover-up is feasible, how many sessions it'll take — flagged for you, never guessed at.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Aftercare stays to your policy</strong>
        <span>It repeats what you've published, word for word. Anything suggesting infection or a reaction goes to a human right away, with no advice attached.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Your voice, your rules</strong>
        <span>Deposit terms, shop minimum, what you will and won't tattoo — it runs on your answers, so it sounds like your studio and not like a chatbot.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

